.Dd February 27, 2026
.Dt FIND 1
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm find
.Nd search for files in a directory hierarchy
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm find
.Op Fl H | Fl L
.Op Ar path ...
.Op Ar expression
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility recursively descends the directory tree for each
.Ar path
listed, evaluating an
.Ar expression
composed of primaries and operators for each file in the tree.
.Pp
If no
.Ar path
is specified,
.Nm
searches the current directory.
If no
.Ar expression
is given, the
.Fl print
primary is implied.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl H
Follow symbolic links on the command line only.
Symbolic links encountered during traversal are not followed.
.It Fl L , Fl follow
Follow all symbolic links.
.El
.Ss Global Options
Global options affect overall behavior and must appear before
any path operands or primaries.
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl depth
Process each directory's contents before the directory itself.
The
.Fl delete
primary implies
.Fl depth .
.It Fl maxdepth Ar n
Descend at most
.Ar n
levels below the starting points.
.Fl maxdepth Ar 0
means only apply tests to the starting points themselves.
.It Fl mindepth Ar n
Do not apply any tests or actions at levels less than
.Ar n .
.Fl mindepth Ar 1
means process all files except the starting points.
.El
.Ss Primaries
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl name Ar pattern
True if the last component of the pathname matches
.Ar pattern
using shell glob syntax
.Pq Sq * , Sq \&? , Sq Op ...  .
.It Fl iname Ar pattern
Like
.Fl name
but the match is case insensitive.
.It Fl path Ar pattern
True if the full pathname matches
.Ar pattern
using shell glob syntax.
Also available as
.Fl wholename .
.It Fl type Ar c
True if the file type matches
.Ar c ,
where
.Ar c
is one of:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Cm b
block device
.It Cm c
character device
.It Cm d
directory
.It Cm f
regular file
.It Cm l
symbolic link
.It Cm p
named pipe (FIFO)
.It Cm s
socket
.El
.It Fl size Ar n Ns Op Cm cwbkMG
True if the file uses
.Ar n
units of space, rounded up.
The default unit is 512-byte blocks.
Suffixes:
.Cm c
(bytes),
.Cm w
(2-byte words),
.Cm b
(512-byte blocks),
.Cm k
(kilobytes),
.Cm M
(megabytes),
.Cm G
(gigabytes).
Prefix
.Ar n
with
.Sq +
for greater than or
.Sq -
for less than.
.It Fl empty
True if the file is a regular empty file or an empty directory.
.It Fl newer Ar file
True if the current file was modified more recently than
.Ar file .
.It Fl mtime Ar n
True if the file was modified
.Ar n
days ago (measured in 24-hour periods).
Prefix
.Ar n
with
.Sq +
for more than
.Ar n
days ago, or
.Sq -
for less than
.Ar n
days ago.
.It Fl perm Ar mode
True if the file permission bits exactly match the octal
.Ar mode .
.It Fl user Ar name
True if the file belongs to user
.Ar name .
A numeric UID is also accepted.
.It Fl group Ar name
True if the file belongs to group
.Ar name .
A numeric GID is also accepted.
.El
.Ss Actions
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Fl print
Print the full pathname followed by a newline.
This is the default action if no other action is specified.
.It Fl print0
Print the full pathname followed by a NUL character.
Useful with
.Xr xargs 1
.Fl 0 .
.It Fl delete
Delete the matched file or empty directory.
Implies
.Fl depth .
.It Fl exec Ar command Brq {} ;
Execute
.Ar command
for each matched file.
The string
.Sq {}
is replaced by the current pathname.
The command must be terminated by an escaped semicolon
.Pq Sq \e; .
.El
.Ss Operators
Primaries may be combined with the following operators,
listed in order of decreasing precedence:
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pq Ar expression
Parentheses for grouping.
Must be escaped or quoted to prevent shell interpretation.
.It Fl not Ar expression
.It Sq "!" Ar expression
Logical NOT.
True if the expression is false.
.It Ar expression Fl and Ar expression
.It Ar expression Fl a Ar expression
Logical AND (default between adjacent primaries).
True if both expressions are true.
.It Ar expression Fl or Ar expression
.It Ar expression Fl o Ar expression
Logical OR.
True if either expression is true.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std find
.Sh EXAMPLES
Find all C source files under the current directory:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ find . -name "*.c"
.Ed
.Pp
Find empty files and directories in /tmp:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ find /tmp -empty
.Ed
.Pp
Find files larger than 1 megabyte, modified in the last 7 days:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
$ find . -type f -size +1M -mtime -7
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ls 1 ,
.Xr xargs 1
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.Nm
utility is compliant with the
.St -p1003.1-2008
specification.
.Pp
The primaries
.Fl iname ,
.Fl path ,
.Fl empty ,
.Fl print0 ,
.Fl delete ,
.Fl maxdepth ,
and
.Fl mindepth
are extensions to that specification.
.Sh AUTHORS
.An "vibeutils implementation by Travis Cole"
